def row(c, v, verdict, prose): R[(c, v)] = (verdict, prose)

row(14, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SHALL NOT EAT ANY CARCASS; TO THE SOJOURNER WITHIN YOUR GATES YOU SHALL GIVE IT THAT HE MAY EAT IT, OR SELL IT TO A FOREIGNER; FOR YOU ARE A HOLY PEOPLE TO THE LORD YOUR GOD. YOU SHALL NOT BOIL A KID IN ITS MOTHER\'S MILK. {HP(14, 21, (("לא", "תאכלו", "כל", "נבלה"), "you shall not eat any carcass — the plural"), (("לגר", "אשר", "בשעריך", "תתננה", "ואכלה"), "to the sojourner within your gates you shall give it that he may eat it — ONE seat; the singular"), (("או", "מכר", "לנכרי"), "or sell it to a foreigner — the Torah\'s two seats of the word"), (("לא", "תבשל", "גדי", "בחלב", "אמו"), "you shall not boil a kid in its mother\'s milk — THE THIRD AND LAST SEAT"))} {AP(14, 21, (("לתותב", "ערל"), "to the UNCIRCUMCISED sojourner — the resident alien supplied, 104:2\'s reading"), (("לבר", "עממין"), "to a son of the peoples — the foreigner"), (("לא", "תיכול", "בשר", "בחלב"), "you shall not eat FLESH WITH MILK — Onkelos writes the law, not the verse; the English\'s bracket"))} THE VERSE OF THREE LAWS: the carcass given not cast (104:1-6\'s table and R. Judah\'s dissent), the holiness clause a second time (104:7), the kid\'s three seats three ways (104:8-10; 76:7\'s eating at 12:24). The register\'s one mixed verse (asserted).')
row(14, 22, 'MATERIAL', f'TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE ALL THE YIELD OF YOUR SEED THAT COMES FORTH FROM THE FIELD YEAR BY YEAR. {HP(14, 22, (("עשר", "תעשר"), "tithe, you shall tithe — the doubling ONE seat; the starred tithe token the parser marks"), (("את", "כל", "תבואת", "זרעך", "היצא", "השדה"), "all the yield of your seed that comes forth from the field — the one article-participle"), (("שנה", "שנה"), "year by year — ONE seat"))} {AP(14, 22, (("עשרא", "תעשר"), "tithe, you shall tithe — doubled in the Aramaic"), (("שתא", "בשתא"), "year in year"))} THE TITHE\'S LAW: 105:1-19\'s liabilities from the verse\'s six clauses — the year, the edible, the field, the pulses, the seller and the buyer.')
row(14, 23, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD IN THE PLACE WHICH HE SHALL CHOOSE TO CAUSE HIS NAME TO DWELL THERE, THE TITHE OF YOUR GRAIN, YOUR WINE AND YOUR OIL AND THE FIRSTLINGS OF YOUR HERD AND YOUR FLOCK, THAT YOU MAY LEARN TO FEAR THE LORD YOUR GOD ALL THE DAYS. {HP(14, 23, (("ואכלת", "לפני", "יהוה", "אלהיך"), "and you shall eat before the LORD your God — ONE seat in this form"), (("במקום", "אשר", "יבחר", "לשכן", "שמו", "שם"), "in the place which He shall choose to cause His name to dwell there — THE PLACE FORMULA\'s fourth seat"), (("מעשר", "דגנך", "תירשך", "ויצהרך"), "the tithe of your grain, your wine and your oil — 12:17\'s list"), (("למען", "תלמד", "ליראה"), "that you may learn to fear"))} {AP(14, 23, (("לאשראה", "שכנתיה", "תמן"), "to cause His SHEKHINAH to dwell there — the formula\'s rendering at nine seats"), (("למדחל", "קדם", "יי"), "to fear before the LORD"))} THE EATING AT THE PLACE: 106:2-5\'s firstling and second tithe compared (the wall, the House standing, the year passed); 106:6\'s study.')
row(14, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'AND WHEN THE WAY IS TOO LONG FOR YOU, THAT YOU ARE NOT ABLE TO CARRY IT, BECAUSE THE PLACE IS TOO FAR FROM YOU WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD SHALL CHOOSE TO PUT HIS NAME THERE, BECAUSE THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL BLESS YOU — {HP(14, 24, (("וכי", "ירבה", "ממך", "הדרך"), "and when the way is too long for you — 19:6\'s twin; the chapter\'s one case on when"), (("כי", "לא", "תוכל", "שאתו"), "that you are not able to carry it"), (("כי", "ירחק", "ממך", "המקום"), "because the place is too far from you — 12:21\'s clause"), (("לשום", "שמו", "שם"), "to put His name there — the formula\'s second form"), (("כי", "יברכך", "יהוה", "אלהיך"), "because the LORD your God will bless you"))} {AP(14, 24, (("וארי", "יסגי", "מנך", "ארחא"), "and when the way is much for you"), (("לאשראה", "שכנתיה", "תמן"), "to cause His Shekhinah to dwell there — the Aramaic\'s one rendering for both forms"))} THE CONDITION: 107:1-3 — place not time, any distance, the rich too.')
row(14, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'THEN YOU SHALL TURN IT INTO MONEY AND BIND UP THE MONEY IN YOUR HAND AND GO TO THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD SHALL CHOOSE. {HP(14, 25, (("ונתתה", "בכסף"), "then you shall turn it into money — the first money"), (("וצרת", "הכסף", "בידך"), "and bind up the money in your hand — ONE seat; the second money"), (("והלכת", "אל", "המקום", "אשר", "יבחר"), "and go to the place which He shall choose"))} {AP(14, 25, (("ותתן", "בכספא", "ותצור", "כספא", "בידך"), "and give in money and bind the money in your hand"))} THE MONEY: 107:4\'s coin with a figure or a thing bound (two arms), 107:5\'s possession, 107:6\'s Shiloh and the House.')
row(14, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL BESTOW THE MONEY ON WHATEVER YOUR SOUL DESIRES — ON OXEN, ON SHEEP, ON WINE, ON STRONG DRINK, ON WHATEVER YOUR SOUL ASKS OF YOU — AND EAT THERE BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD AND REJOICE, YOU AND YOUR HOUSEHOLD. {HP(14, 26, (("ונתתה", "הכסף", "בכל", "אשר", "תאוה", "נפשך"), "and bestow the money on whatever your soul desires — the third money; the verb\'s one Torah seat"), (("בבקר", "ובצאן", "וביין", "ובשכר"), "on oxen, on sheep, on wine, on strong drink — the Torah\'s six seats of strong drink, here permitted"), (("ובכל", "אשר", "תשאלך", "נפשך"), "on whatever your soul asks of you — ONE seat"), (("ושמחת", "אתה", "וביתך"), "and rejoice, you and your household — ONE seat"))} {AP(14, 26, (("ובחמר", "חדת", "ועתיק"), "on wine NEW AND OLD — the strong drink read as aged wine; the English\'s bracket"), (("ותחדי", "את", "ואנש", "ביתך"), "and rejoice, you and the people of your house"))} THE SPENDING: 107:7\'s three moneys, 107:8-11\'s class (not slaves or land; the condiments; not water or salt), 107:12-15\'s containers, 107:16\'s rejoicing a peace offering.')
row(14, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE LEVITE WITHIN YOUR GATES, YOU SHALL NOT FORSAKE HIM, FOR HE HAS NO PORTION NOR INHERITANCE WITH YOU. {HP(14, 27, (("והלוי", "אשר", "בשעריך", "לא", "תעזבנו"), "and the Levite within your gates you shall not forsake him — 12:19\'s warning in a new form, no token in order"), (("כי", "אין", "לו", "חלק", "ונחלה", "עמך"), "for he has no portion nor inheritance with you — the Levite\'s five seats"))} {AP(14, 27, (("לא", "תשבקניה"), "you shall not leave him"), (("חלק", "ואחסנא", "עמך"), "portion and inheritance with you"))} THE LEVITE: 108:1\'s ladder of four; 108:2\'s cause.')
row(14, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'AT THE END OF THREE YEARS YOU SHALL BRING OUT ALL THE TITHE OF YOUR PRODUCE IN THAT YEAR AND LAY IT UP WITHIN YOUR GATES. {HP(14, 28, (("מקצה", "שלש", "שנים"), "at the end of three years — THE NUMBER VERSE [3]; Samaria\'s fall the one kin"), (("תוציא", "את", "כל", "מעשר", "תבואתך"), "you shall bring out all the tithe of your produce — 26:12\'s clause"), (("בשנה", "ההוא", "והנחת", "בשעריך"), "in that year, and lay it up within your gates"))} {AP(14, 28, (("מסוף", "תלת", "שנין"), "from the end of three years — the number carried"), (("ותצנע", "בקרויך"), "and store it in your cities"))} THE THIRD YEAR: 109:1-3\'s date (Passover\'s last day of the fourth and the seventh), 109:4-5\'s one tithe, 109:7-9\'s bringing out.')
row(14, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE LEVITE SHALL COME, FOR HE HAS NO PORTION NOR INHERITANCE WITH YOU, AND THE SOJOURNER AND THE FATHERLESS AND THE WIDOW WITHIN YOUR GATES, AND THEY SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED, THAT THE LORD YOUR GOD MAY BLESS YOU IN ALL THE WORK OF YOUR HAND WHICH YOU DO. {HP(14, 29, (("ובא", "הלוי", "כי", "אין", "לו", "חלק", "ונחלה"), "and the Levite shall come, for he has no portion nor inheritance"), (("והגר", "והיתום", "והאלמנה", "אשר", "בשעריך"), "and the sojourner, the fatherless and the widow within your gates — THE FOUR AT THE GATE, the formula\'s first seat"), (("ואכלו", "ושבעו"), "and they shall eat and be satisfied — ONE seat in this form"), (("למען", "יברכך", "יהוה", "אלהיך", "בכל", "מעשה", "ידך"), "that the LORD your God may bless you in all the work of your hand — 24:19\'s twin"))} {AP(14, 29, (("וגיורא", "ויתמא", "וארמלא"), "and the convert, the orphan and the widow"), (("וייכלון", "וישבעון"), "and they shall eat and be satisfied"))} THE FOUR: 109:10-12\'s which tithe yields and the poor man\'s gifts exempt; 110:1-4\'s want, covenant, measure and Land.')
